{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/446724-advice-on-what-to-do-when-your-pc-group-spills-the-beans-on-their-solarhood-to-npc-s","id":446724,"title":"Advice on what to do when your pc group spills the beans on their Solarhood to npc's?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-17T17:04:50-07:00","id":446724,"title":"Advice on what to do when your pc group spills the beans on their Solarhood to npc's?","content":"So, my players (a full circle, minus the -Zenith and +Twilight) are reaching that point where they've openly outed themselves as Anathema, and may begin to be taking the fall out for it. They went totemic themselves (well, only our Eclipse really did, but our Night and Dawn were right there in the fight with him and displaying supernatural power) while facing off against a group of summoned Erymanthus that went bananas (Ha!) over an Immaculates protest of said sorcerer's corruption. The whole circle saved a lot of lives, but now I'm trying to figure out what would be the 'fair' way for this to turn out.<br /> <br /> The Immaculates have a strong presence dating back to a Dynast Dragon-blooded heroically dying in the area. It's not a satrapy, however, by virtue of being too far from the Realm, a little to the South East of the Hundred Kingdoms, and officially part of a moderately large nation. Anyway, the small city (Basalt) generally look favorably on the Immaculates, but the nearest Dragonblooded are away in Grey Falls. Game ended pretty much right after the climactic battle, so I'm hoping to give them some way to either get out of this or capitalize on it on the next session.<br /> <br /> Aside from the Immaculates, the people tend to worship gods of field, forest and river, the other major religion in the area is worship of Khasland's patron goddess Sabi-Rohm.<br /> <br /> - - - <br /> <br /> On a more general note, how long do you typically wait before people will generally accept a group of anathema as a not Demon-god-kings? Never? It's weird, I figured I'd be prepared for this moment but I'm finding it difficult to come up with a good answer..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:15:37-07:00","id":446744,"title":"","content":"If I were your player, I would feel that the fairest thing you could do for us given the context would be for the non-immaculates in the area to give us food, supplies and directions to the next city, while promising to stall/mislead the Wyld Hunt as long as possible, while politely insisting we leave before we brought down the fury of the Immaculate Order on our heads.<br /> <br /> It's not a great situation for anyone, but the player's good deeds should be acknowledged and rewarded by those would be grateful for the PCs efforts on their behalf, even if it means they can't stay there anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:28:08-07:00","id":446768,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Personally I would only have a single NPC do the things JayTee said while the rest would be generally skittish and wary around them. Your average peasant would likely just keep their head down and not get involved. As for the Immaculates... I don't think they'd go after the Solars right away since the Sorcerer would be the bigger threat, but they would frostily try to convince them that it'd be better for all involved for them to move along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:00:23-07:00","id":446964,"title":"","content":"They were directly observed by an active Immaculate Monk saving people from the summoned demons of a (DB? Mortal? Celestial?) sorcerer? To be honest, the next scene may be the party &quot;converting&quot; the Immaculate into not wanting to kill them, with just a few social Charms, but somebody from town is gonna be running to the nearest chapter of the Wyld Hunt, though it may be quite a ways out.<br /> <br /> How you want to play it is really up to you, but if the party plays it right, they may need to lay low for a season or two in a Manse situated nearby, but the village would probably support them, especially if they keep supporting the village. Figure that since the nearest Wyld Hunt chapter is Grayfalls, and since you said they are a few hundred miles SE of the Hundred Kingdoms, that means they are probably a good thousand or more from there. That's a good two, maybe three full months just to have the snitch (if there is a snitch) get there, another two or three for the Hunt to even respond, if ever, and then if they do respond in force (and there are loads of reasons political and practical they wouldn't), another month or two for them to get into the region. ANY Solar circle, even lacking in Zenith talkers, should have completely converted even the hardest Immaculates with a minimum of effort, and since the kingdom isn't a Satrapy there aren't gonna be as many hardened Immaculates around beyond the monk that witnessed them directly. The monk they &quot;converted&quot; in the next scene. The monk that is now their biggest supporter. Mwa ha. Mwa hahahaha! And so forth.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if they run roughshod over the village just because they can, even the most mind-wiped villager will eventually revolt when offered the rescue from the inevitable Wyld Hunt when nobody hears from the area for a year or more.<br /> <br /> Your options should be in response to their actions and the overall campaign needs. If you want them to be able to set up a long term power base in or near the village, and their actions are conducive to the villagers WANTING them to stick around, extenuating circumstances keep the Wyld Hunt away until the party has built their power base. If you want them to go globe-trotting, or they are being dictatorial the monk is more than capable of having some secret Immaculate MA ability that allows him to ignore mind control and alert the Wyld Hunt instantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4623-onigato","name":"Onigato","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:58:16-07:00","id":447036,"title":"","content":"I don't think it should be that easy for a Solar circle to convince an Immaculate monk or devout believers that they're safe. They're scary monsters that attacked another scary monster. The villagers are probably grateful or relieved unless the circle have been treating them badly before now. But if the Immaculate faith is a presence in this area, lots of folk will probably be uneasy at best around Anathema. And the monk is probably a harder sell yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T21:13:39-07:00","id":447094,"title":"","content":"If the nearest DBs are off in Grey Falls and it's that far away, I wouldn't worry about the Hunt, possibly ever for that one overstep. The mortal monk shouldn't be too hard to convince, and your eclipse can oathbind him into silence anyway. If it's a small town and the local gods aren't currently getting their faces smashed by Immaculates to keep them in line there's probably not going to be any way word will even get to the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T09:23:31-07:00","id":447796,"title":"","content":"We can assume that Immaculate devotion in this place is shaky, given that the people apparently directly worship local deities. They may be as safe as any of those--or as dangerous.<br /> <br /> Ideally, the Immaculate will shoo them off as best he can, and attempt to avoid engaging them in conversation. One of them bears the mark of the Deceiver, which probably means that they can have the monk prostrating himself before them and blaspheming the Dragons if he actually talks to them and listens to what he has to say. For his soul and hope of Terrestrial reincarnation--and for that of the locals--he <i>cannot</i> allow them to stay. Perhaps challenging them would make him a martyr. Or perhaps it would make an example of him as to why those poor natives should turn to worship the hellspawned soulstealing monsters.<br /> <br /> Do not engage directly, reason says. Repeat, <i>do not engage. </i><br /> <br /> The monk may endeavor to contact the Hunt the moment he gets the chance. But he may also spend some time before he leaves to make sure everyone agrees that the Anathema were terrible things that nearly trampled the people underfoot as their sinful violence and pride clashed.<br /> <br /> I would just be leery of letting this town be swayed easily and wholly. But YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T15:38:08-07:00","id":450951,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice folks. I've elected to have a 2nd of the Immaculates (I prolly didn't communicate fully enough that there are many Immaculates at the shrine. A dozen to a hundred at any one time, around 50 were around to attend the protest, around 40 made it out alive. Anyway) meet with the player and discuss that they and any of the city who wished to go were taking their leave of the Anathema and making way for Grey Falls.<br /> <br /> It helps smooth things over that the Solars captured the sorcerer and delivered him into the Monks keeping.<br /> <br /> The PC's will of course be worried that the monks will inform their activities to a Realm envoy once they get to the satrapy, but it remains to be seen if the monks and their flock make it back to Grey Falls at all. <br /> <br /> As for the rest of the city, they'r too busy fleeing their homes in the wake of a migrating heart Chakra colony (which I expect the Circle to be all over stopping), and will (if they don't bungle it) provide more evidence that the Anathema (or at least <i>these</i> Anathema) are not the monsters they've been led to believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T16:03:45-07:00","id":450963,"title":"","content":"Sounds like you have it well in hand. People in Creation react similarly to people in RL. Treat them well, and they typically don't mind you as a neighbor, once they get used to you. Save their hineys two or three times against the big bad of the week, and they usually LIKE you being around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4623-onigato","name":"Onigato","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:08:23-07:00","id":451064,"title":"","content":"The Immaculates might take the stance it was a staged fight, to trick the locals into believing they are friendly. That's how many Anathemas work; they appear helpfull and kind to lure people into their grasps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}